  "body": "Originally reported in https://github.com/jsdom/jsdom/issues/3513 by @joliss:\r\n\r\nIn at least Chrome and Firefox:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nwindow.history.pushState(null, null, \"/foo/bar#baz\");\r\nwindow.history.pushState(null, null, \"\");\r\nconsole.log(window.document.URL);\r\n// prints: http://localhost:3000/foo/bar#baz\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut per the spec, we parse the empty string relative to the base URL `http://localhost:3000/foo/bar#baz`, which [results in stripping the hash](https://jsdom.github.io/whatwg-url/#url=&base=aHR0cDovL2xvY2FsaG9zdDozMDAwL2Zvby9iYXIjYmF6).\r\n\r\nChromium's special-casing code is [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/history.cc;l=299-301;drc=4baaf6a3dc1c91f711a17d8fb789ad0e71ab2a17). Firefox's is [here](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/ae8629b27d8e0b187ebc1816be0c25bfd68bf955/docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp#11313-11315). WebKit appears to be spec compliant with [no special case](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/f6d05d22b1b873e7fecddb98465ec9b1da40b155/Source/WebCore/page/History.cpp#L178), although I haven't tested it directly yet.\r\n\r\nI'll work on a quick PR to align with the 2/3 behavior.",
